Subject: [PATCH] Complete a Channel Scan Request on its 1905 ACK

Patch 0011 routes a 1905 ACK only to a radio with an unassociated metrics,
steering or policy request outstanding under that MID; any other ACK is
dropped ("find_em_for_msg_type failed"). A Channel Scan Request completes
only on its ACK (em_channel_t::handle_1905_ack), so the radio stayed in
channel_scan_pending and the request went out again every second, as long
as the orchestration lasted (40 s and more after an OpenSync pod rejoined in
a fifty-client room). A radio in that state is not configured: candidate
queries to it were refused with Error_Not_Ready and steers waited, so the
optimizer's snapshot stayed incomplete and the room missed its load window.

Route the ACK to the radio whose scan request carries its MID, and record
that MID before the frame is sent: the agent's ACK can arrive first.

Upstream-Status: Pending

--- a/src/ctrl/em_ctrl.cpp
+++ b/src/ctrl/em_ctrl.cpp
@@ -1476,6 +1476,15 @@
                     em = radio_em;
                     break;
                 }
+                /* The ACK is the only completion of a Channel Scan Request
+                 * (em_channel_t::handle_1905_ack); the report can follow much
+                 * later or carry a failure status. Dropped, the radio stayed in
+                 * channel_scan_pending and the request was resent every second. */
+                if ((radio_em->get_state() == em_state_ctrl_channel_scan_pending) &&
+                    (radio_em->m_chan_req_msg_id == response_msg_id)) {
+                    em = radio_em;
+                    break;
+                }
             }
 
             if (em == NULL) {
--- a/src/em/channel/em_channel.cpp
+++ b/src/em/channel/em_channel.cpp
@@ -623,12 +623,14 @@
         //return -1;
     }
 
+    // Known before the frame leaves: the agent's 1905 ACK can arrive first.
+    m_chan_req_msg_id = ntohs(cmdu->id);
     if (send_frame(buff, len)  < 0) {
         em_printfout("Channel Scan Request msg failed, error:%d", errno);
+        m_chan_req_msg_id = 0;
         return -1;
     }
 
-    m_chan_req_msg_id = ntohs(cmdu->id);
     em_printfout("Channel Scan Request message sent (msg_id: 0x%04x)\n", m_chan_req_msg_id);
 
     return  static_cast<int> (len);
